    {"text": "Recognize y = (x+1)^2 as a composite function gof(x) = g[f(x)] and use a value table to observe its limit as x approaches 0.", "source_id": "provided-pdf-2025-10-01-00007213", "source_page": 9}
  ],
  "source_formulas": [
    {"expression": "y = (x + 1)^2, composed as f: x -> x + 1, g: x -> x^2", "source_id": "provided-pdf-2025-10-01-00007213", "source_page": 9},
    {"expression": "gof(x) = g[f(x)]", "source_id": "provided-pdf-2025-10-01-00007213", "source_page": 8},
    {"expression": "lim (3x^2 - 21)^(1/3) as x -> 4 = 3", "source_id": "provided-pdf-2025-10-01-00007213", "source_page": 10}
